# Another harness regenerates this as a COPY of CLAUDE.md, which drifted and
# corrupted within a day (claude.ai connectors rewritten as "Codex.ai", the
# self-reference rewritten to cite itself). One instruction file lives in
# exactly one place: CLAUDE.md. Removed 2026-08-26, regenerated, removed again
# 2026-08-27 and ignored so it can never become tracked truth.
AGENTS.md

# The SAME harness, the same failure, found 2026-08-30: a copy of
# `.claude/skills/consult-room/SKILL.md` with the one instruction it carries
# rewritten from `rfa connect claude-code --skill` to `rfa connect Codex
# --skill`, which is not a command - it falls through to the usage text
# (measured). The tracked skill is the one in `.claude/`, generated from
# `templates/skills/consult-room/SKILL.md` by `rfa connect claude-code --skill`;
# a second copy is a second truth, and this one was already wrong. Removed and
# ignored, exactly as AGENTS.md was.
.agents/

# Local MCP wiring for whichever host the operator runs here: a URL and a port
# on THIS machine (`localhost:8790` is the owner's hub), regenerated by the tool
# that owns it. Machine state, never project source - the same reason no hub
# directory's `.rfa/` is tracked.
.codex/
